          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.549,
            0.026,
            0.846,
            0.043
          ],
          "content": "Chapter 10 — Light: Mirrors and Lenses"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.888,
            0.029,
            0.922,
            0.044
          ],
          "content": "159"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.093,
            0.551,
            0.117
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 10.5: Let us experiment"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.136,
            0.549,
            0.211
          ],
          "content": "z Use the same setup as in Activity 10.4, but place a stiff sheet of chart paper flat on a table such that part of it extends beyond the edge of the table."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.213,
            0.549,
            0.287
          ],
          "content": "z Shine a beam of light on the mirror placed on the sheet and observe the reflected beam on the extended portion (Fig. 10.10a)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.288,
            0.548,
            0.363
          ],
          "content": "z Now, bend the extended part of the sheet along the edge of the table (Fig. 10.10b). Do you still see the reflected beam on the extended portion?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.365,
            0.516,
            0.384
          ],
          "content": "z Flatten the paper again and observe."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.385,
            0.549,
            0.498
          ],
          "content": "The reflected beam disappears when the sheet is bent but reappears when it is flattened again. This shows that the reflected beam lies in the same plane as that of the incident beam. Bending the sheet creates a new plane, breaking this alignment."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.498,
            0.549,
            0.574
          ],
          "content": "**The incident ray, the normal to the mirror at the point of incidence, and the reflected ray, all lie in the same plane**. This is another law of reflection."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.579,
            0.139,
            0.891,
            0.303
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
